.TH "YAMLR-DEMO" "1" "May 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
yamlr-demo \- Propose repairs and remediate Kubernetes manifests.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBInteractive Demo Generator\fR
.PP
Scaffolds a \fByamlr-demo/\fR directory containing intentionally broken manifests. This is designed for first-time users to safely test \fByamlr scan\fR and \fByamlr heal\fR without risking their own files.
.PP
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.RS
yamlr demo
.RE
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Creates:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fByamlr-demo/broken-deployment.yaml\fR: Syntax errors, missing selectors.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fByamlr-demo/legacy-ingress.yaml\fR: Deprecated APIs.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fByamlr-demo/.yamlr.yaml\fR: Sample config.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
.RS
yamlr demo
cd yamlr-demo
yamlr scan .
yamlr heal .
### Global Performance Flags
Available across all commands:

*   **`--timing`**: [PERFORMANCE] Output surgical execution timing breakdown.
*   **`--timing-file <FILE>`**: [PERFORMANCE] Save performance profiling data to a JSON file.
.RE
.fi
.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/yamlr/yamlr/issues>
.PP
